352
00:17:10,460 --> 00:17:12,300
And I just made up my best move yet!

353
00:17:12,580 --> 00:17:14,480
I call this one the gum-gum balloon!

354
00:17:14,820 --> 00:17:17,540
It can bounce back cannonballs and bullets and lots of stuff!

355
00:17:17,920 --> 00:17:18,400
Whoa!

356
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:19,820
Can you show me right now?

357
00:17:20,040 --> 00:17:20,420
Sure!

358
00:17:20,520 --> 00:17:21,600
I'll do it just for you!

359
00:17:22,080 --> 00:17:23,880
That meanie doesn't get to see it!

360
00:17:24,220 --> 00:17:25,040
Don't peek!

361
00:17:25,040 --> 00:17:26,700
Here we go!

362
00:17:27,200 --> 00:17:28,900
Gum-gum!

363
00:17:33,900 --> 00:17:34,380
Dude!

364
00:17:34,600 --> 00:17:35,500
That's nuts!

365
00:17:35,880 --> 00:17:36,960
You keep getting bigger!

366
00:17:37,260 --> 00:17:38,520
You're not going to pop, are you?

367
00:17:39,060 --> 00:17:40,740
Oh-oh!

368
00:17:41,120 --> 00:17:42,020
Oh-oh!

369
00:17:42,160 --> 00:17:44,140
Everything bounces right off!

370
00:17:44,820 --> 00:17:47,300
Well, not sure I'd use the word cool.

371
00:17:47,300 --> 00:17:50,760
And you bounce right off my foot!

372
00:17:52,820 --> 00:17:53,420
Sabo!

373
00:17:53,560 --> 00:17:54,580
Kick him back here!

374
00:17:55,480 --> 00:17:56,600
Oh-uh-huh?

375
00:17:59,500 --> 00:18:00,820
Gum-gum balloon!

376
00:18:01,100 --> 00:18:02,000
You're right, Luffy!

377
00:18:02,180 --> 00:18:03,960
Your gum-gum moves are pretty neat!

378
00:18:04,660 --> 00:18:05,480
Gum-gum!

379
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:06,460
Hey!

380
00:18:06,580 --> 00:18:09,520
If you can block cannonballs, then try blocking this!

381
00:18:09,520 --> 00:18:11,520
Gum-gum balloon!

382
00:18:11,940 --> 00:18:12,520
Ah!

383
00:18:12,520 --> 00:18:12,980
Ah!

384
00:18:15,980 --> 00:18:16,860
Ah!

385
00:18:18,040 --> 00:18:18,960
Whoa!

386
00:18:19,420 --> 00:18:19,940
Ah!

387
00:18:25,040 --> 00:18:25,640
Ah!

388
00:18:26,280 --> 00:18:29,600
Wait, you can't just eat a guy then run away like that!

389
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:32,220
Astam out!

390
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:33,660
Ah!

391
00:18:37,500 --> 00:18:38,920
Gu-guys!

392
00:18:41,480 --> 00:18:41,920
Ha-ha!

393
00:18:41,920 --> 00:18:48,120
Yeah, sometimes that happens, right?

394
00:18:48,120 --> 00:18:48,940
No, it doesn't!

395
00:18:49,080 --> 00:18:50,560
I almost got eaten back there!

396
00:18:50,620 --> 00:18:51,740
Don't try to play it off!

397
00:18:51,740 --> 00:18:52,340
Get over it.

398
00:18:52,420 --> 00:18:55,060
We got lots of crocodile meat for dinner, so it worked out.

399
00:18:55,620 --> 00:18:57,480
Mmm, good point!

400
00:18:57,900 --> 00:18:59,920
Uh, that was fast.

401
00:19:00,720 --> 00:19:03,420
But I want to have some crocodile right now!

402
00:19:03,720 --> 00:19:05,260
I can't wait till dinner!

403
00:19:05,820 --> 00:19:06,280
Ace!

404
00:19:06,620 --> 00:19:06,780
Hmm?

405
00:19:07,160 --> 00:19:10,320
Uh, before we get back to the hag's place, I want to check something.

406
00:19:10,320 --> 00:19:11,960
Can you come with me?

407
00:19:21,960 --> 00:19:23,180
See anything in there?

408
00:19:23,440 --> 00:19:24,520
Look carefully!

409
00:19:25,460 --> 00:19:28,380
Man, it's a good thing we moved our pirate savings.

410
00:19:28,640 --> 00:19:28,900
Yeah.

411
00:19:29,500 --> 00:19:31,820
While we're at it, you want to check Grey Terminal, too?

412
00:19:32,180 --> 00:19:33,040
Good idea.

413
00:19:33,640 --> 00:19:35,640
Ace, Luffy, you two head back.

414
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:36,440
I'll catch up.

415
00:19:36,440 --> 00:19:36,720
Ah!

416
00:19:37,660 --> 00:19:38,000
Ah!

417
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:42,500
He won't listen to anyone.

418
00:19:48,360 --> 00:19:49,600
Good grief!

419
00:19:49,840 --> 00:19:53,180
This place is swarming with the usual punks and Blue Jams guys.

420
00:19:53,660 --> 00:19:55,020
And they mean business.

421
00:19:55,880 --> 00:19:57,420
Well, what did you expect?

422
00:19:57,740 --> 00:20:00,020
Blue Jams got to be super pissed right now.

423
00:20:00,020 --> 00:20:03,460
Huh?

424
00:20:04,740 --> 00:20:05,700
Hey, guys!

425
00:20:05,980 --> 00:20:07,960
Those kids you've been looking for are right here!

426
00:20:08,180 --> 00:20:09,160
All three of them!

427
00:20:09,380 --> 00:20:09,720
What?

428
00:20:10,720 --> 00:20:11,640
He's right!

429
00:20:11,760 --> 00:20:12,280
Grab them!

430
00:20:12,400 --> 00:20:12,960
Give it up!

431
00:20:13,220 --> 00:20:15,960
There's a bounty on your head and I've got to catch it in!

432
00:20:18,020 --> 00:20:18,460
Huh.

433
00:20:21,360 --> 00:20:22,720
Well, that just sucks.

434
00:20:22,860 --> 00:20:25,380
Blue Jams got all of Grey Terminal hunting us down.

435
00:20:25,560 --> 00:20:26,980
We'd better lay low for now.

436
00:20:27,120 --> 00:20:28,140
There's too many of them.

437
00:20:28,400 --> 00:20:30,740
Here's hoping they get bored and move on to something else.

438
00:20:31,460 --> 00:20:32,700
Why should we hide?

439
00:20:33,020 --> 00:20:35,140
If they find us, then we can just fight them.

440
00:20:35,260 --> 00:20:36,940
That's no reason to pick a fight, though.

441
00:20:37,260 --> 00:20:37,560
What?

442
00:20:37,600 --> 00:20:40,140
Are we going to beat up like a hundred guys just because?

443
00:20:40,760 --> 00:20:41,240
Yay!

444
00:20:41,600 --> 00:20:42,360
Stubble's right!

445
00:20:42,560 --> 00:20:44,260
Nobody asked you.

446
00:20:48,260 --> 00:20:49,140
Blue Jams?

447
00:20:49,140 --> 00:20:51,220
The kids sure know how to screw us over.

448
00:20:51,740 --> 00:20:54,680
I'm sure those pirates are going to find out about this place pretty soon.

449
00:20:55,100 --> 00:20:55,580
Oh, man.

450
00:20:56,040 --> 00:20:57,420
We're going to be in big trouble.

451
00:20:58,100 --> 00:21:01,100
We're tough, but no way we can beat Blue Jams, man.

452
00:21:01,440 --> 00:21:03,980
Maybe this is the end of the Dadan family.

453
00:21:04,300 --> 00:21:06,020
We've had a great run, guys.

454
00:21:06,280 --> 00:21:09,920
But it's time to say goodbye to the Mountain Bandit's life.

455
00:21:10,780 --> 00:21:13,740
All of our crimes are coming back to bite us in the ass.

456
00:21:14,180 --> 00:21:14,900
Live by the sword.

457
00:21:15,020 --> 00:21:15,860
Die by the sword.

458
00:21:16,100 --> 00:21:17,380
We should have known.

459
00:21:17,380 --> 00:21:20,260
Had a great run?

460
00:21:20,480 --> 00:21:21,460
We can't beat them?

461
00:21:21,640 --> 00:21:23,820
How pathetic can you numbskulls get?

462
00:21:24,060 --> 00:21:27,320
Don't you take any pride in being Mountain Bandits all these years?

463
00:21:27,860 --> 00:21:29,020
This is simple.

464
00:21:29,920 --> 00:21:32,200
If they come by asking for the brats,

465
00:21:32,460 --> 00:21:36,360
we'll just hand Ace and Luffy and that stupid new kid right on over.

466
00:21:36,620 --> 00:21:38,800
Yeah, but boss, there's Garp.

467
00:21:38,980 --> 00:21:40,640
He'll get angry at us if we do that.

468
00:21:41,100 --> 00:21:43,360
Plus, that Blue Jam guy's a monster.

469
00:21:43,500 --> 00:21:45,540
If he finds out we even know those kids,

470
00:21:45,620 --> 00:21:47,240
he'll kill us just for the hell of it.

471
00:21:47,380 --> 00:21:51,820
Well, then...

472
00:21:51,820 --> 00:21:52,640
Yes?

473
00:21:54,800 --> 00:21:56,080
Then we'll play dumb.

474
00:21:56,360 --> 00:21:58,320
Yeah, just pretend we don't know them.

475
00:21:58,600 --> 00:22:00,100
Now, let's try it.

476
00:22:00,240 --> 00:22:01,100
Be real dumb.

477
00:22:02,100 --> 00:22:02,780
Hey, guys.

478
00:22:02,980 --> 00:22:04,260
Have you seen Ace and Sawbo?

479
00:22:04,640 --> 00:22:05,500
They stay in here?

480
00:22:05,960 --> 00:22:06,900
Spit it out or else.

481
00:22:07,100 --> 00:22:08,320
We don't know.

482
00:22:08,320 --> 00:22:12,840
That was bad.

483
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:13,940
Boss!

484
00:22:14,280 --> 00:22:14,820
Boss!

485
00:22:15,160 --> 00:22:17,080
Ace and those other brats are back.

486
00:22:17,080 --> 00:22:17,340
Huh?

487
00:22:17,340 --> 00:22:17,380
Huh?

488
00:22:17,380 --> 00:22:32,120
Fearing for his life,

489
00:22:32,360 --> 00:22:35,620
Sabo left Grey Terminal and found a home with Ace and Luffy,

490
00:22:36,020 --> 00:22:37,620
much to Dedan's dismay.

491
00:22:37,620 --> 00:22:42,140
For the three unwanted guests, it was a never-ending party.

492
00:22:43,080 --> 00:22:45,740
Making any excuse to get out of their daily chores,

493
00:22:46,000 --> 00:22:47,940
they hunted wild animals in the mountains,

494
00:22:48,420 --> 00:22:50,120
tussled with hooligans in the city,

495
00:22:50,440 --> 00:22:52,300
and dueled with pirates of the cove.

496
00:22:53,600 --> 00:22:57,640
Within time, news of their wild exploits reached far and wide,

497
00:22:57,640 --> 00:23:01,100
even over the high walls surrounding the center of the kingdom.

498
00:23:10,200 --> 00:23:14,280
Luffy, Ace, and Sawbo make a name for themselves in Grey Terminal.

499
00:23:14,820 --> 00:23:16,740
While celebrating their latest victory,

500
00:23:17,160 --> 00:23:19,680
a surprising truth about Sawbo is revealed,

501
00:23:20,120 --> 00:23:22,140
and the boys make a promise to one another

502
00:23:22,140 --> 00:23:24,160
that will shape their future.

503
00:23:24,160 --> 00:23:27,980
On the next, One Piece, to the sea someday!

504
00:23:28,420 --> 00:23:29,980
The Pledge of the Three Brats!

505
00:23:30,500 --> 00:23:32,320
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

